\f0\fs24 \cf0 water well: pumps water up, has 1 output connection \
water filtration building: makes it clean for use: future nodes and pipes have less calcification (which causes leaking), has 2 connections\
hub: can transform all pipes into all other pipes, has 6 connections,\
T split: has 3 connections, can transform all pipes into all others\
pump: 2 connections, greatly increases the possible length of connected pipes\
binder: very short range, but allows multiple identical links to and from other nodes: eg: to double the flow from a well to a power plant, you can place 4 binders between them, which allows 2 massive pipes to be laid from the well to the power plant using the binders as intermediate (needed) nodes. you can upgrade these to allow 3, 4 or even 5 pipes side by side (very expensive and late game). \
\
power: can be generated with nuclear power plants, water turbines (which needs a river), windmills (on land or sea), and sun panels (need to be imported);\
power uses voltage and ampere: high voltage when created, low voltage when delivered and needs transformers to change between them. ampere is how much (you know how it works, make it realistic).\
transformer: extermely short range, but acts as a hub with 6 connections and can change any voltage into any other voltage.\
the range of power lines is determined by its voltage: high voltage can travel further. (if the same is true for water pipes and water pressure, you should implement that also)\
electricity can also leak, because of degrading lines. \
use power versions of the water distribution, i dont know much about it but you do , so make sure the electricity grid is realistic and doesn't just copy water pipes.\
\
Oil: when pipes leak, they pollute the region, with quantity of the leak determining the extremity : big cargo ship leaks a lot: very bad, small oil pipe: a bit bad.\
environmental science lab: is needed to keep the rivers, and natural water sources clean (if dirty, no water is produced), should be placed near the oil rig (digging site) to keep a massive area (like 9 regions, so this one and all adjacent ones) clean for water and soil (for farming)\
\
farm: uses a large amount of land to grow crops, and keep livestock animals (for food: eggs, milk, pork, chicken, beef etc), requires a lot of water and some oil and electricity}